      "id": 1,
      "text": "McKinney sits on Kentucky Route 198 and the Norfolk Southern Railway, just 8.6 miles southwest of Stanford.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McKinney%2C_Kentucky",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Archibald McKinney, a Revolutionary War veteran, founded McKinney's Fort around 1790 with four cabins and a stockade on high ground nine miles southwest of Logan's Station.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://explorekyhistory.ky.gov/items/show/574",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "McKinney's Fort later became McKinney's Station, a key trading post on the Cumberland Trace that supplied the local militia against Native American incursions.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://explorekyhistory.ky.gov/items/show/574",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A historical marker (No. 2063) in Lincoln County commemorates McKinney's Fort as an early Kentucky settlement and trading post.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://explorekyhistory.ky.gov/items/show/574",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Frontier forts like McKinney's were often named after their founders, offering settlers protection and peace of mind.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://explorekyhistory.ky.gov/items/show/574",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Log forts and stockades appeared across the Bluegrass Region from the mid-1770s into the 1790s, marking rapid frontier expansion.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
